{
  "_doc": "#1274 The permission catalogue read by libs:perms PermCatalogue: the ONE list the Permissions page draws, auto-requests, checks and generates the ADB block from. Feature libs declare what they need through `features` here and PermsNeeds.missing(ctx, feature); they never ask or open settings themselves. kind: runtime (system dialog) | special (a settings toggle) | appops (an app-op) | adb_only (only pm grant / shell can set it). section: runtime | special | battery | samsung | adb (page order). A runtime entry that the app's manifest does not declare reads 'not applicable'. settings.action opens the exact page; package_uri adds package:<pkg>; highlight_key goes in :settings:fragment_args_key (scroll + highlight where Settings supports it); samsung_component is tried first on Samsung. adb: shell commands without the 'adb shell' prefix; {pkg} {listener} {a11y} {admin} are filled per device, a line with an unknown value is dropped.",
  "_doc_contract_libs": "Every lib under ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs (each Gradle lib's src/main) is held to the contract by PermsOnePlaceTest: none may request a permission, start a permission settings page or write a pm grant line; each goes through PermsNeeds + PermsLink (or PermsShell / PermsPages / PermsGrant for shell grants and App info). contract_allowlist names the only exceptions: libs:perms itself, which implements the asking. A lib with no PermsHost page in its app lands on PermsActivity, which libs:perms merges into every app that embeds it.",
  "contract_allowlist": ["perms"],
  "group_order": ["NOTIFICATIONS", "LOCATION", "NEARBY_DEVICES", "CAMERA", "MICROPHONE", "CONTACTS", "CALENDAR", "PHONE", "SMS", "STORAGE", "ACTIVITY", "SENSORS", "LOCATION_BACKGROUND"],
